                                        "responseId": "0035a9a8-1862-4e64-8b9e-5c5d274b1f58",
                                        "response": "<p>Nasdaq Boardvantage is an online platform used to share association documentation and facilitate communication between the management company and association board members. It serves primarily as a portal to support board meetings by providing access to key documents such as financial statements, meeting minutes, and relevant government materials. These documents are made available to assigned board members and management personnel, who can open, view, and interact with them directly through the portal.</p><p><br></p><p>The platform enables users to facilitate meetings remotely, annotate and markup documents, and assign permissions for viewing or editing. Documents are posted to a shared location within designated team spaces, each of which has an owner who can grant access rights. Boardvantage also tracks which documents are being viewed by users who log in.</p><p><br></p><p>Access to the portal is managed through SSO for MVW members, while board members use password-based login. When a new board member is added, an internal notification triggers coordination with Boardvantage, which then sends a setup link to the new member. It is the member’s responsibility to complete their account setup.</p><p><br></p><p>The team is requesting 710 licenses to support approximately 210 Associates and 500 board members, both domestic and international. There will be two global administrators overseeing the platform, and each association will have a local site admin responsible for managing access specific to their location. The documents shared within the portal include association-related financial statements and other governance materials.</p>",
